        {
            "number": 6,
            "revision": "a480b89a32772ec4e7b243a90fa34892dea97a54",
            "parents": [
                "c796cab5a2d381640da5deeb428a4af682b69a19"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/55/80255/6",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Unive Tien",
                "email": "unive.tien.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "UniveTien"
            },
            "createdOn": 1748240412,
            "author": {
                "name": "Unive Tien",
                "email": "unive.tien.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "UniveTien"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/firmware_update.h",
                    "line": 2095,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "This change only passes CI because the struct isn't captured in the ABI dump as the related functions are still marked as `LIBPLDM_ABI_TESTING`. It's not a sustainable change to make.\n\nI'm working on making the API/ABI for the package iterators support multiple package formats in a sustainable way."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/firmware_update.h",
                    "line": 2095,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Unive Tien",
                        "email": "unive.tien.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "UniveTien"
                    },
                    "message": "Not quite sure the meaning, as this is a mandatory field for v1.3.0, I didn't find an reachable approach for supporting that without adding this field, otherwise we're bypassing this in the implementation.\n\nJFYI: I have an outdated patch for testing purpose, which transfer all of these to `LIBPLDM_ABI_STABLE` and passed CI: [#80559]\n\n[#80559]: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/libpldm/+/80559"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/firmware_update.h",
                    "line": 2095,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "So to make sure we have things crisp here, while DSP0267 v1.3.0 specifies e.g. header format revision 4, it also (implicitly) specifies header format revisions 3, 2 and 1. From my perspective it's valid to use DSP0267 v1.3.0 to implement support for e.g. revision 2, and still not yet support revision 4.\n\nTo implement format revision 4, yes, we need to add e.g. the reference manifest data field. Now that my iterator patch introduces the pin concept, we can do that with confidence that we won't cause invalid memory accesses on behalf of the application when upgrading or downgrading the library."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/firmware_update.c",
                    "line": 684,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Does the code initialize the struct var to '\\0' somewhere because i am wondering if you need to set \nrec->reference_manifest_data.ptr = NULL \n\nin case !rec->reference_manifest_data.length as on line# 715."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/firmware_update.c",
                    "line": 684,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Unive Tien",
                        "email": "unive.tien.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "UniveTien"
                    },
                    "message": "Received, will apply this to the next patchset."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/firmware_update.c",
                    "line": 3206,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Does the code initialize the struct var to '\\0' somewhere because i am wondering if you need to set\nrec->reference_manifest_data.ptr = NULL\n\nin case !rec->reference_manifest_data.length as on line# 715."
                },
